# TradingView 9 EMA Full Candle

## Source
- Source: [[sources/tradingview-mechanical-strategy-scripts]]
- Page / Timestamp: TradingView script `9 EMA First Full Candle Entry + EMA Cross Exit (Strategy)`, author handle `myttthew`, open-source strategy, page shows Feb 10, accessed 2026-05-22, https://www.tradingview.com/script/zTbBxN70-9-EMA-First-Full-Candle-Entry-EMA-Cross-Exit-Strategy/

## Mechanics

### Entry
Use M5 baseline.

- Compute EMA(9).
- Long setup:
  - Current candle closes fully above EMA(9): low > EMA(9).
  - This is the first qualifying candle after price was not fully above EMA(9).
  - No existing position.
- Short setup:
  - Current candle closes fully below EMA(9): high < EMA(9).
  - This is the first qualifying candle after price was not fully below EMA(9).
  - No existing position.

### Exit
- Exit long when price crosses back below EMA(9).
- Exit short when price crosses back above EMA(9).
- V5 safety stop: ATR(14) * 1.5 or recent swing beyond entry candle.

### Stop Loss
- Source-visible text uses EMA cross exit only.
- V5 baseline hard stop: min of 1.5 * ATR(14) and entry-candle opposite extreme plus 0.25 ATR buffer.

### Position Sizing
V5 default: fixed-risk $1,000 for P2 baseline, one position per symbol/magic.

### Zusatzliche Filter
- Session-time gate: liquid session only for scalping baseline.
- Optional trend filter with EMA(50) can be tested later, not baseline.
- Friday close flatten and news blackout from V5 framework.

## Concepts (what kind of strategy is this)
- [[concepts/intraday-trend-continuation]] - requires full candle clearance of EMA(9).
- [[concepts/moving-average-filter]] - EMA(9) defines both entry and exit state.
- [[concepts/scalping]] - source is designed for 5-minute intraday execution.

